From b0a70d610edff6999edd59307f8c28035dde8021 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Konstantinov <alex.konstantinov@stfc.ac.uk>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 07:43:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(#72): keep the canonical STAR input immutable and pin
 its trusted digest

Codex review finding on PR110 (discussion r4119221898, P2) at f9650704,
confirmed by inspection and fixed once here as the integration owner.

The defect. test-data/generate_known_motion_fixture.py wrote each case's .star
unconditionally, before the canonical block, and the canonical block validated
only movie_sha256. MANIFEST.json carried no STAR digest and verify_fixtures.py
hashed only the movie and the ground-truth JSON. So a STAR_TEMPLATE change that
alters _rlnMicrographOriginalPixelSize, _rlnVoltage or _rlnMicrographMovieName
moves no pixel: the CI order (preflight -> generate --canonical ->
verify_fixtures -> run_known_motion_gates --no-regenerate) rewrote the committed
STAR, then passed canonical verification, then ran the known-motion gates on
freshly generated metadata. That is precisely the bit-exact parity gate this
fixture set exists to provide.

Two independent halves, because either one alone leaves a hole:

1. Generator. Canonical mode now compares the generated STAR against the
   committed file and refuses on disagreement with a unified diff, instead of
   writing it -- symmetric with how it already treats the ground-truth JSON, and
   the committed file is left byte-identical on disk. A missing STAR in
   canonical mode is an error, as a missing truth JSON already is. Normal
   (non-canonical) generation is unchanged and still writes.

2. Manifest and verifier. Every case gains star_sha256, required by
   validate_manifest_schema and verified per case alongside the movie and truth
   digests. This covers the path that bypasses the generator entirely: CI runs
   the gates with --no-regenerate, so a STAR altered on disk would otherwise
   never be hashed by anything.

MANIFEST.json changes are additive only -- every existing movie_sha256,
movie_bytes and ground_truth_sha256 is untouched, and the new digests are
computed from the STAR files as already committed. No hash was loosened and no
gate or tolerance was relaxed; requiring star_sha256 is a tightening that fails
closed on a manifest that lacks it.

Ownership: #72/PR102 owns these three files. Fixed once here to avoid a
duplicate implementation; reusable patch mapping is published for PR102 rather
than applied there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
